      "description": "Watch Trabzonspor vs Galatasaray highlights and goals from Süper Lig on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 28, 2026. The Süper Lig clash between Trabzonspor and Galatasaray on August 28, 2026 , lived up to its billing as a high-stakes encounter. Both sides displayed immense energy from the start, setting the stage for a match that would be defined by pivotal refereeing decisions and clinical finishing. Early Drama and the Breakthrough The match took a dramatic turn in the 13th minute when Ruslan Malinovsky was shown a straight red card, leading to heated protests from his teammates. The numerical shift allowed the attacking side to capitalize quickly. In the 19th minute, Adam Nagy provided a brilliant assist for Callum O'Dowda , who kept his cool to slot the ball home and open the scoring. The first half remained physical, highlighted by a yellow card for Stefan Savic shortly after the dismissal. Second Half Surge and Red Card Chaos The intensity ramped up after the interval following several tactical substitutions. In the 54th minute, Marius Corbu doubled the lead with a well-placed strike. However, the disciplinary narrative continued as Sidny Lopes Cabral was sent off in the 57th minute after receiving his second yellow card. The pressure resulted in a penalty in the 59th minute, which Bamidele Yusuf clinicaly converted after Andre Onana was booked for the preceding foul. Late Impact and Final Whistle As the clock ticked down, fresh legs were introduced, including Naby Keita and Krisztian Lisztes . It was Lisztes who made the final mark on the scoresheet in the 86th minute, finishing off a move orchestrated by Oliver Nagy . Although Lisztes picked up a yellow card in the 88th minute, the damage was already done. The referee blew the final whistle at 90+2 minutes, ending a chaotic and enthralling contest that saw multiple goals and dismissals."
